  "_unresolved_why": "An indirect call no rule, signature or vtable resolves is charged 512 B below it: what is left after the rows below are shallow hooks (UART putc, ring-buffer copies, pin detach callbacks, std::function holding a plain pointer). The report counts them; a deep one must get a row.",
  "terminal": [
    {
      "function": "^(abort|__assert_func|esp_system_abort|panic_abort|esp_panic_handler|std::terminate\\(\\)|__cxxabiv1::__terminate\\(void \\(\\*\\)\\(\\)\\)|__cxa_pure_virtual|__cxa_deleted_virtual|_exit|esp_restart|esp_restart_noos)$",
      "why": "never returns: the device restarts. The bytes it takes decide only how the panic reads, so the gate counts its own frame and stops there"
    }
  ],
  "impossible_calls": [
    {
      "caller": "^esp_cache_get_alignment$",
      "callee": "^esp_log$",
      "why": "its only log is ESP_RETURN_ON_FALSE(out_alignment, ..., \"null pointer\") (esp_mm/esp_cache_msync.c), and its only caller here, esp_heap_adjust_alignment_to_hw, passes the address of a local"
    },
    {
      "caller": "^mbedtls_ssl_handshake_step$",
      "callee": "^mbedtls_ssl_(tls13_)?handshake_server_step$",
      "why": "every TLS context on the device is a client: ssl_client.cpp's mbedtls_ssl_config_defaults(..., MBEDTLS_SSL_IS_CLIENT, ...); the server step runs only for MBEDTLS_SSL_IS_SERVER"
    },
    {
      "caller": "^(ssl_check_ctr_renegotiate|ssl_handle_hs_message_post_handshake|mbedtls_ssl_read|mbedtls_ssl_write)$",
      "callee": "^(mbedtls_ssl_renegotiate|mbedtls_ssl_start_renegotiation)$",
      "why": "renegotiation stays at mbedTLS's default MBEDTLS_SSL_RENEGOTIATION_DISABLED: nothing in the firmware or its libraries calls mbedtls_ssl_conf_renegotiation, and both callers return before renegotiating when it is disabled"
    }
  ],
  "_aliases_why": "Typedefs and macros the source uses for a class: FileImplPtr and FSImplPtr are shared_ptrs of fs::FileImpl and fs::FSImpl (FS.h); WiFiClient(Secure) are the Arduino 3 names of NetworkClient(Secure); Serial is HWCDCSerial on these boards (ARDUINO_USB_CDC_ON_BOOT=1, ARDUINO_USB_MODE=1 in platformio.ini)",
  "stdout_context": {
    "entries": "^(vprintf|printf|puts|putchar|esp_log_writev|esp_log_write)$",
    "family": "^(_vfprintf_r|vfprintf|__sbprintf|_fflush_r|fflush|__sflush_r|__swrite|_write_r|write|__sfvwrite_r|__sprint_r|_putc_r|__swbuf_r|_puts_r|_putchar_r|__sinit|__smakebuf_r|__swsetup_r|_fwrite_r|esp_vfs_write|console_\\w+)$",
    "files": "^(vfs_fat|vfs_littlefs)_",
    "why": "printf, puts and esp_log write the console stream (stdout, fd 1, the console VFS over USB serial or UART); a file write never runs below them, so inside that stream's stdio calls the VFS reaches the console devices only"
  }
}